# HELP - Browse online help

```text
HELP [topic [section]] [/S=filespec] [/R]
```

## Reading topics

Type `HELP` to open the default archive. An authored index opens first.
When the archive has no index, choose a topic from its member list.

`HELP PIP` opens the PIP topic. `HELP PIP SELECTORS` opens
[PIP selectors](PIP.HLP#selectors) directly.

Press the digit or letter shown beside a section or link. Within a topic,
`.` or `>` advances one page and `,` or `<` goes back one page.
Press Q or Ctrl-C to return one level. At the top level either key exits
to the command prompt.

## Finding a topic

A named request searches the current drive/user and [PATH](PATH.HLP) for
loose help files, then checks the first HELP.LBR and the first HELP.ARK.
Within a location, plain HLP takes precedence over squeezed HQP and
crunched HZP. To see the actual source, type:

```text
HELP PIP /REPORT
```

## Choosing a source

`/S=` is short for `/SOURCE=`. Specify an archive to browse its contents
or a loose file to read that exact copy.

```text
HELP /S=A15:HELP.ARK
HELP PIP /S=A15:HELP.ARK /R
HELP /S=B3:PIP.HQP
```

You can [build a custom help library](NOAH.HLP#help-libraries) from your own topics.
